WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.910
- Narrator: You've been bitten!

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:04.450
And, uh-oh, it's venomous.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:05.970
How long have you got?

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.310
Well, that depends on a few factors,

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:12.000
including the potency, dose delivered,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.150
and speed of distribution.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.900
Turns out, not all
venoms act the same way.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:18.980
Here are the animals

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.663
with the fastest acting venom on earth.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.460
First up, spiders.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.660
There are around 40,000 species of spider

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.800
and most are venomous.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.901
But, thankfully, only a handful
pose a threat to humans,

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:39.830
including the male
Sydney Funnel-web Spider.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.940
Its venom is 60 times as potent as cyanide

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.880
and can kill a human in one to two hours.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.200
The venom attacks the nervous system,

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.560
kicking it into overdrive until,
ultimately, it shuts down.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.500
Of course, spiders aren't the only

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.740
venomous animals in Australia.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:03.690
It's home to 20 of the
world's 25 deadliest snakes,

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:07.860
including the Eastern Brown
Snake which is responsible

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.920
for the most snakebite
deaths in the country.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.320
Its venom is 8,000 times
stronger than cyanide

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:18.890
and can kill a human in about one hour.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:22.330
Its venom also attacks
the central nervous system

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.840
but, this time, it slows everything down.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.690
And, to top it off, the
venom has a coagulant

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:31.920
that causes the blood in your
veins and arteries to clot.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.380
Between the two, it's
not a good way to go.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:38.360
Now, at this point, you
might consider switching

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:41.530
your Australian safari to a scuba dive,

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.910
just to be on the safe side.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:47.990
But, venomous animals live
in Australian waters too,

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.580
like the Blue-ringed Octopus.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:55.090
Its venom is 1,000 times
more toxic than cyanide

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.730
and it'll bring down a human
in just 20 to 40 minutes.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:04.070
Bacteria in its saliva makes
an extremely potent neurotoxin

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.210
which paralyzes your muscles.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.990
And, once that paralysis
hits your diaphragm

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:12.180
and rib muscles, you
have only a few minutes

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.113
before you suffocate to death.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.530
But another marine
animal is even deadlier.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.800
The fastest acting venom on earth

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.600
belongs to the Australian
Box Jellyfish, or Sea Wasp.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.070
It's not the most potent venom out there

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:31.210
at 2,000 times stronger than cyanide,

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.550
but encounter one of these guys

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:36.840
and you'll be dead in 15 minutes.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.660
That's because their tentacles are covered

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.240
with tiny, venom loaded
darts called nematocysts,

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.220
which shoot heart-stopping
toxins into the body

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.360
wherever they make contact.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.720
All of this sounds pretty
scary but, remember,

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.620
you're less likely to
die by venomous spider

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:58.430
than by car crashes and
infection, or disease.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:01.620
And, it's not like these
animals are after you anyway.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.010
They'd just as well prefer

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.780
that you stick to your own habitat.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:10.200
But, still, be smart,
be respectful, be safe.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.960
Tell us the scariest animal
encounter you've ever had,

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.223
and thanks for watching.

